# =========================================================================
#  .gitignore — workstream-fleetmonitor
#
#  ALLOWLIST, not a denylist: line 1 of the rules is `*`, so EVERYTHING is
#  ignored unless it is opted back in under section 1.
#
#  Deliberately inverted: this repo sits next to secrets.json, .env.local,
#  a plaintext fleet password and 100MB+ of generated report data. With a
#  normal denylist, any new secret or dump is committed by default and you
#  find out afterwards. Here a new file has to be opted in on purpose.
#
#  Adding a file to the repo?  ->  section 1, add a `!` rule.
#  Something generated getting committed?  ->  sections 2c-2f.
#
#  CONTENTS
#    1.  Allowlist — the only things that ARE committed
#        1a. Source
#        1b. Config / manifests
#    2.  Re-ignored after the allowlist (later rules win)
#        2a. Local-only working directory
#        2b. Secrets — never commit
#        2c. Vendored / build output
#        2d. Runtime state written by fleet_monitor.py
#        2e. Generated reports — csv + raw json dumps
#        2f. Generated logs
#        2g. OS noise
#
#  Companion file: .vercelignore, which trims the deployment bundle.
#  Both are listed in README.md under "Repository layout".
# =========================================================================
*

# Descend into directories so the rules below can match inside them.
!*/


# ── 1a. Source ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!.gitignore
!.vercelignore
!*.py
!*.html
!favicon.ico
# Static assets served from public/. Without these the allowlist silently
# drops them and a GitHub-sourced build ships without the PWA/service worker.
!public/*.js
!public/*.png
!public/*.webmanifest
!*.md

# Dashboard suggestions and the status set against each by hand. Not generated
# — it is edited and deployed, and the API reads its statuses back out.
!feedback.txt


# ── 1b. Config / manifests ───────────────────────────────────────────────
!pyproject.toml
!requirements.txt
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!vercel.json
!fly.toml
!Dockerfile
!.dockerfile


# =========================================================================
#  2. Re-ignored AFTER the allowlist, because later rules win. Without this,
#  `!*.py` above would happily pull in every .py inside node_modules.
# =========================================================================

# ── 2a. Local-only working directory ─────────────────────────────────────
# Runtime caches, generated logs, secrets, and the unused Fly.io/Docker/npm
# leftovers. Ignored wholesale — the allowlist above would otherwise pull in
# local/package.json, local/*.md and every .py under local/node_modules.
local/


# ── 2b. Secrets — never commit ───────────────────────────────────────────
secrets.json
.env
.env.*
*.local
categorize_config.txt
query_config.txt


# ── 2c. Vendored / build output ──────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.vercel/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/


# ── 2d. Runtime state written by fleet_monitor.py ────────────────────────
# Rebuilt automatically from the fleet API. Committing it causes merge
# conflicts and puts operator names into git history.
.daily_hours_cache.json
.dashboard_sessions.json
.frame_health_cache.json
.leaderboard_cache.json
.pi_session_cache.json
.task_history.json
.device_locations.json
*.tmp


# ── 2e. Generated reports — csv + raw json dumps ─────────────────────────
# Output of categorize_tasks.py and query_tasks.py. Every one of these is
# reproducible by re-running the script, and between them they are 100MB+ of
# session data carrying operator names — nothing that belongs in git history.
#
# The allowlist above already ignores them by default; these rules are
# written out anyway so the intent survives someone adding a broad `!` rule.
*.csv
*.raw.json
task_report*.json
task_report*.csv
query_report*.json
query_report*.csv
# Root-level dump of the fleet API's session listing.
sessions.json


# ── 2f. Generated logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
operator_sessions/
recording_logs/
daily_recording_log_*.txt
operator_sessions_*.txt
*.log


# ── 2g. OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
